course: dictionary
lesson: 3027
title: Words for keenness
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Eagerness is a noun. It means a strong wish to do or have something, with lots of energy and interest. It also means keenness, being impatient to start. Someone with eagerness cannot wait to begin.
explain: «She put her hand up in her eagerness to help.» The word eagerness tells you how she felt: happy, excited and ready to act. You can see eagerness in someone's face, voice and quick movements.
explain: Eagerness is good in school, and teachers praise «eagerness to learn». But too much eagerness can make a character rush and make mistakes. Toad's eagerness for every new craze often got him into trouble.
fact: Eagerness is an uncountable noun, so you say «a lot of eagerness», not «two eagernesses».
fact: «Eagerness» means a strong wish to do or have something, full of energy and interest.
fact: «Eagerness» also means keenness, being impatient to start.
fact: «Eager» is the adjective: «eager to learn» means keen to learn.
fact: In the Just So Stories, the Elephant's Child's eagerness to know what the Crocodile has for dinner gets him into trouble.
exercise: «She jumped up in her eagerness to help.» What does eagerness mean here? | *A strong wish to help, full of energy | Being very tired | Being bored and slow | Being angry with the class
exercise: Mrs Patel writes in a report: «Ravi shows great eagerness to learn.» What is she praising? | Ravi is good at drawing | Ravi is always late | Ravi is sleepy in class | *Ravi is keen and full of energy for learning
exercise: Which word means nearly the same as eagerness, the feeling of being keen to start? | Boredom | Fear | Sleepiness | *Keenness
test: In stories, eagerness often makes a character do what? | Forget their name | Fall asleep | Sit still and wait | *Rush and make mistakes
test: Which word is the noun from eager? | eagerous | *eagerness | eagerly | eagered
exam: A child writes: «Her eagerness to learn made her the first to finish.» What does this tell you about her? | She did not want to learn | She was tired and wanted to go home | *She was keen and full of energy for learning | She was angry with her teacher
